    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0034" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/1–2944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Interior</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ickes</hi>)<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d17-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-31">January 31,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I wish to advise you of
                    my approval of the outline of principles of the proposed agreement, dated
                    January 24, <pb facs="0035" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/> 1944, covering the proposed
                    pipeline from the Persian Gulf area to a port on the eastern Mediterranean, with
                    the revisions made therein at the meeting of the Directors of the Petroleum
                    Reserves Corporation on January 27, 1944.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d17-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d17-f1" n="24" type="source" xml:id="d17-f1-content">
                <p>This letter was addressed to Mr. Ickes in his capacity as President of the
                    Petroleum Reserves Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d17-f2" n="25" xml:id="d17-f2-content">
                <p>At a meeting of the Board of Directors of the Petroleum Reserves Corporation on
                    February 5, 1944, Mr. Ickes submitted an additional paragraph (No. 11) which had
                    been drafted at President Roosevelt’s direction. Mr. Rayner notified Mr. Ickes
                    the same day of the approval of the additional paragraph by the Secretary of
                    State (800.6363/2–544). The date January 24 was retained on the outline as
                    finally approved. A summary was released on February 6, 1944, by the Department
                    of the Interior (800.6363/2–644); for substance of the press release, see
                    telegram 437, March 3, 1 p.m., to Cairo, <ref target="#pg24">p. 24</ref>. The
                    texts of the outline and of the press release are printed in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Congressional Record</hi>, vol. 90, pt. 2, p. 1466.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
